{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"=== HANDOFF #20 — SESSION END (context exhausted). READ THIS, THEN #19 + ITS ADDENDUM, THEN #18 + ADDENDA 1-3. ===\n\nBOARD, verified at writing (do not trust it — re-read the tickets):\n  e369 **32/35**. OPEN: 2b16, 88d9, 5200 (all in_progress).\n  3e73 **5/6** — ALL FOUR P1 CHILDREN CLOSED plus 0fad. Only P2 2127 remains. **DO NOT START 2127.**\n  gerrit/main @ b6916709f3. In flight: **change 1288 (88d9), LLM-Review +1, awaiting Verified.**\n\n--- IMMEDIATE NEXT ACTIONS, in order ---\n 1. **Submit 1288** once `Verified +1` arrives (`POST /a/changes/1288/submit -d '{}'`). If it shows a `-1`,\n    diagnose BEFORE reacting: check whether `build-and-test` actually RAN\n    (`gh run view <id> --repo navapbc/rebar --json jobs`). Two of its `-1`s this session were NOT real —\n    one was a cancelled run with `build-and-test` SKIPPED. Its ONE real failure is already fixed.\n 2. **Then implement 2b16's arbitration fix.** Plan is AMENDED and RE-CERTIFIED (0 blocking). It was\n    serialized behind 1288 because both touch `inbound_differ.py`.\n 3. **Then close 88d9** (`--class preexisting`; it is a bug ticket, `--class` is required).\n 4. **Then re-run the harness** — `gh workflow run external-integration.yml --repo navapbc/rebar --ref main`,\n    job `jira-dc-harness`, ~24 min. The last run (30784592232) PREDATES all four merges since, and the suite\n    grew 56 -> 58 cells.\n 5. **Then close 5200** (18 ACs, already independently verified — see its AC-verification comment; the\n    outstanding work is the RUN, not the analysis), then **close e369** (13 ACs verified: 11 MET, AC1 blocked\n    only by the children, AC5 already AMENDED; **its plan review is `stale-code` and MUST be re-run first**).\n\n--- THE ONE THING TO CARRY ABOVE ANY TICKET ---\n**A MERGED, MUTATION-CHECKED FIX DID NOT WORK, AND THE FAULT WAS THE SPECIFICATION.** 2b16's change 1276 is\non main and its feature can never fire: my G4 rule suppressed an inbound removal whenever outbound was\nadding that target, but a peer deletion ALWAYS produces an outbound ADD. Its unit suite was green and\nmutation-proven throughout, because `test_g4_outbound_add_this_pass_suppresses_the_removal` asserted exactly\nwhat the plan said. **A mutation ledger proves the code matches the plan; it cannot prove the plan is\nright.** Only the live harness caught it. For anything with a live oracle, the harness is the arbiter — a\ngreen unit suite is necessary and NOT sufficient. This is now an explicit AC on 2b16.\n\n--- WHAT THE HARNESS RUN BOUGHT (worth the 24 minutes) ---\nRun 30784592232, `collected=56 executed=56 skipped=0`, 4 failed / 52 passed:\n  * **751e VERIFIED LIVE** (`test_outbound_unassign_round_trips` PASSED).\n  * 2b16 refuted (above).\n  * **PLATFORM UNKNOWN SETTLED: DC REFUSES to null a sub-task's `fields.parent`** — HTTP 400\n    `{\"errors\":{\"parent\":\"data was not an object\"}}`. So 88d9's live cell may legitimately end at\n    `SETUP FAILED`; that is the platform branch its AC anticipates, **NOT the fix failing.** Do not\n    \"repair\" the cell.\n  * **39c1 CONFIRMED LIVE** (`test_outbound_clear_parent_round_trips`): outbound parent ops cannot be\n    emitted for DC. It was filed off a code reading; it is now observed. It is filed as NOT gating e369\n    (consistent with the operator's e39f ruling) but flagged BORDERLINE because, unlike e39f, it does not\n    fail safe. **The operator may want to revisit that now it is confirmed live.**\n\n--- DECISIONS ON THE RECORD (do not silently re-decide) ---\n  * OPERATOR: 5200's row-12-OUTBOUND was to be BUILT, not amended → done, merged (1283).\n  * OPERATOR: e39f is a follow-up, does NOT gate e369 (it fails safe).\n  * MINE: 39c1 filed NOT gating, flagged BORDERLINE (see above).\n  * MINE: 049e closed with ONE AC amended, not ticked — it demanded an EMPIRICAL determination and the\n    answer is DOCUMENTARY (the harness is amd64-only and never comes up on this arm64 host). Justified\n    because the remedy is INDEPENDENT of the answer and the probe is DEFERRED to 275e, not dropped.\n  * MINE: e369's AC5 AMENDED — it demanded \"exactly one implementation reachable by both backends\" for the\n    rich-text codec and identity model, an outcome that would be WRONG (ADF vs wiki; accountId vs name).\n\n--- PROCESS ERRORS I MADE. THEY ARE RULES NOW. ---\n 1. **A green targeted test slice is NOT enough before pushing.** I pushed 1288 on 287 green unit tests and\n    it failed CI on an integration contract. Run `tests/integration/rebar_reconciler/` too, and DO the\n    consumer sweep — grep BOTH `\"x\" in fields` AND `fields[\"x\"]` forms. 88d9's own AC named that risk.\n 2. **A change sitting in review DECAYS.** CI takes the WORKFLOW from main but the CODE from the patchset, so\n    when main adds a workflow step invoking a NEW script, older-based changes fail on a missing FILE that\n    reads like a broken main or a flake. Bitten TWICE (`check_config_reads.py`, then `probe_rebar.py`). **On a\n    missing-file failure under `scripts/`, REBASE — never recheck.** I wasted a cycle rechecking. Diagnose\n    with `git ls-tree -r --name-only gerrit/main -- <path>`; `git cat-file -e` in a loop MISREPORTS and once\n    made me believe main itself was broken for everyone.\n 3. `recheck-review` re-triggers the LLM bot but **ALSO re-runs CI and CLEARS `Verified +1`** (dispatch matches\n    the `recheck` substring). Never fire it across a stack or while a run is in flight — doing so caused a\n    cancellation and a bogus `-1`. The bot usually catches up on its own; prefer patience.\n 4. A `flock: could not acquire lock after 60s` error can be reported while the write ACTUALLY LANDED, and an\n    immediate re-read can show stale content. Pause, re-read, THEN decide, or you duplicate the comment.\n 5. Subagents STALLED TWICE on the `wt-88d9` worktree (watchdog, 600s). **Script bounded mechanical work —\n    mutation ledgers especially — INLINE.** The stalls cost nothing only because the agent had committed.\n 6. Never `git reset --soft gerrit/main` in an older-based worktree — it sweeps in others' landed commits.\n    Reset to the explicit base SHA; check `git show --stat HEAD` for YOUR commit (a `git diff --stat\n    gerrit/main` showing extra files usually just means main advanced).\n 7. `git commit --amend -F -` regenerates the Change-Id; pass a file that still CONTAINS the Change-Id line.\n\n--- WORKTREES ---\n  /Users/joeoakhart/rebar-jira-family  main working tree (branch worktree-main)\n  /Users/joeoakhart/agent-5200-diag    parked FOR CLOSES — `git merge --ff-only gerrit/main` first;\n                                       `--ref` does NOT satisfy the file_impact close precheck\n  /Users/joeoakhart/wt-88d9            88d9's branch (change 1288). Backups of the FIXED files: /tmp/88d9-bak/\n  /Users/joeoakhart/wt-2b16, /Users/joeoakhart/wt-5200b  branches merged; reusable for the 2b16 fix\n\n--- FOLLOW-UPS FILED, NONE GATING e369 ---\n  275e (empirical application-properties probe, deferred from 049e) · 59b2 (live-suite assertions that cannot\n  fail) · e39f (inbound link removal never converges for a two-relation pair) · 6c0a (extract the issuelinks\n  enrichment so 2b16's G1 test stops hand-mirroring production) · 39c1 (outbound parent-set unreachable on\n  DC — CONFIRMED LIVE) · plus earlier: cabc, a3fa, d582, 9fb3, 63e8, 3b5f."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1785770626024241001,"uuid":"2b7e349e-2573-4596-9ce6-d66976261364"}